==Galician==

===Etymology===
From Old Galician and {{inh|gl|roa-opt|eis}} (13th century, {{w|Cantigas de Santa Maria}}), from {{inh|gl|la|ixe}} or {{m|la|isse}}, non-standard variants of {{m|la|ipse||himself}} and cognate to {{cog|an|eix|ex, eix, eis}}, {{cog|osp|eje}}, {{cog|ca|eixe}}, {{cog|oc|eis}} ({{cog|pro|eps}}), {{cog|fro|es|es, esse}}.<ref>{{cite-book|title=The Cambridge history of the Romance languages. Volume 1, Structures|date=2011|publisher=Cambridge University Press|location=Cambridge|url=https://www.worldcat.org/oclc/765006720|isbn=978-0-511-78013-4|oclc=765006720|page=478}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|en|author=Konstanze Jungbluth|title=Manual of Deixis in Romance Languages|year=2015|publisher=Walter de Gruyter GmbH & Co KG|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=_AE_CwAAQBAJ&pg=PT865&lpg=PT865|url2=http://media06.euv-frankfurt-o.de/Literatur/Jungbluth,%20Konstanze_Da%20Milano_Federica_2015_Manual%20of%20Deixis%20in%20Romance%20Languages_Cap%2022.pdf|isbn=978-3-11-039356-9|author2=Federica Da Milano|page=553}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|/ˈejs/}}

===Interjection===
{{head|gl|interjection}}

# {{lb|gl|formal}} [[behold]]!
#* '''1671''', Gabriel Feixoo, ''Contenda dos labradores de Caldelas'':
#*: '''''es''''aquí mandereita,''
#*: ''e digo que deijemola endeita''.
#*:: '''Here you have''' my right hand;
#*:: I say: let's leave this task.
#* '''1671''', Gabriel Feixoo, ''Contenda dos labradores de Caldelas'':
#*: ''Labrador:''
#*: ''ò rio, ò rio co'eles.''
#*: '''''eis''' uns a cabalo doutros.''
#*:: Farmer:
#*:: "Let's we throw them to the river."
#*:: "'''Here they are''' [Watch them], the ones atop the others."
#: {{uxi|gl|'''Ei'''la tes, noviña do trinque|'''Here''' you have it, brand new}}
#: {{syn|gl|velaquí|velaí}}

====Usage notes====
This word can contract with articles and pronouns.

